3. Tools/terminal: view.rs:1171 uses the toolkit ToolCall/status/disclosures;
   bridge.rs:462 loads the entire completed terminal blob and decodes it on a
   blocking worker. tests/gui_rich.rs:221 pauses a real shell at a file barrier,
   asserts rendered TOOL role, LIVE-TAIL and Running status mid-stream, then
   asserts all 10000 payload words plus BLOB-END after completion.
4. Approval: view.rs:1296 uses the approval atom, with stable rendered actions,
   keyboard selection and distinct green Allow/red Deny surfaces. window.rs:228
   routes navigation and Escape; cancel resolves Deny with reason Cancelled.
   tests/gui_rich.rs:536 uses actual gateway prompts and keyboard/Escape actions,
   including cancellation while a slash popup is open. gui_bridge's rendered
   Allow/Always/Deny actions still send ResolveApproval on the control lane.
   A retired rendered approval is rejected locally before dispatch; the API
   witness asserts no stale operation reached the durable gateway log.
   Plan, Image, Usage and Subagent retain readable plain text.
5. Composer: editor.rs owns the upgraded toolkit Editor while retaining composer
   presentation/submission. History Up at the first logical line and draft
   restoration are tested at tests/gui_rich.rs:175. Both / and @ request hooks
   are exposed; offered completions are /interrupt and /stop only. No file search.
   Completion actions retain their request token; a stale popup cannot replace
   newer typing (tests/gui_rich.rs:593).
6a. The real Bridge::replay -> publish_frame -> state.prepared path is tested at
   tests/gui_rich.rs:73 with >64 KiB and real MarkdownPrepare permit calls.
   It reads prepared_on_ui == false; R15 checks one shared rt/UI-core registry.
6b. No 4 KiB cap: retained full rows and visible glyph filtering (view.rs:932)
   allow the long reply's END-OF-LONG-REPLY to be read at the bottom of an 860px
   viewport (gui_rich.rs:94). A separate long single-line code case activates
   the source disclosure and reads its ending through vertical scrolling (:504).
6c. verification/README.md:68 and :88 correctly distinguish 100k worker protocol
